@title 3D: the wire heat fold stays when no wires are routed and says why, and the EMC button says it is off
@area 3D
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# The hot cabinet fixture has no routed wires. After a run the Heat panel keeps its "Wire heat in the ducts" fold and, opened, says either no wires are routed or none has a known current (it used to vanish). Hovering the EMC button in the 3D toolbar reads "Off: ... Click to show it", so the dim button is seen as a switch that is off, not a disabled one. Both are drawn text the harness cannot read, so the pictures are the evidence.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
click_text Heat #1
wait 20
click_text "Settings for the next run"
wait 10
click_text Quick
wait 10
click_text Simulate #2
wait_s 150
expect_not "Locked while the run goes"
expect "Wire heat in the ducts"
click_text "Wire heat in the ducts"
wait 10
expect "route them first"
shot 01-wire-heat-fold
check_layout
move 299 218
wait 20
shot 02-emc-hint
check_blank 02-emc-hint
